{"name":"Diminutive Pink","hex":"#f1dede","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diminutive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very small.","Serving to diminish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A word form expressing smallness, youth, unimportance, or endearment.","The smallest, thinnest version of a traditional heraldic ordinary (\"geometric shape on a shield\"), often used to represent multiple instances of a charge or to modify a main, central, and larger charge; not itself modifiable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diminutive"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diminutive","blocks":[{"text":"A diminutive is a word obtained by modifying a root word to convey a slighter degree of its root meaning, either to convey the smallness of the object or quality named, or to convey a sense of intimacy or endearment, and sometimes to belittle something or someone. A diminutive form is a word-formation device used to express such meanings. A double diminutive is a diminutive form with two diminutive suffixes rather than one."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diminutive","wikidata":"Q108709"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"ht